# Implementation Plan - Phase F: Monsoon and Low-Pressure-System Reliability (Gate 5 / P1)

Phase F implements the **Monsoon and Low-Pressure-System (LPS) Reliability Specialist (`MONSOON_RELIABILITY_V1`)**, covering:
1. **Low-pressure systems, depressions, deep depressions, and monsoon depressions**
2. **Active and break monsoon regimes**
3. **System dynamics failure** (system location $> 200$ km, propagation speed $> 5$ km/h, deepening $> 4$ hPa)
4. **Precipitation failure** (rainfall placement $> 100$ km, rainfall intensity $> 50$ mm/24h)
5. **Regime-transition failure** (unstable active $\rightarrow$ break or break $\rightarrow$ active shifts)

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Three-Pillar Decomposition**: Monsoon reliability will NOT be collapsed into one opaque score. It explicitly decomposes into:
>   - System Dynamics Reliability (location, speed, deepening)
>   - Precipitation Reliability (rainfall placement, intensity)
>   - Regime Transition Reliability (active $\leftrightarrow$ break stability)
> - **Anti-Leakage**: Strictly issue-time features at $t_0$ (SLP, 850-hPa wind, vorticity, moisture transport, vertical shear). Ground truth observations (IMD gridded rainfall, RSMC monsoon bulletins) sealed with 24h verification latency.
> - **Regime-Slice Validation**: Performance is verified separately across active monsoon, break monsoon, and transition periods.

